---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';

const project = {
  title: 'Failed Rain Barrels → Compost Barrels',
  status: 'In Progress',
  started: 'Spring 2026',
  specs: [
    { label: 'Barrels', value: '2' },
    { label: 'System', value: 'Dual Rotation' },
    { label: 'Aeration Holes', value: '20 per barrel' },
    { label: 'Turn Schedule', value: 'Weekly (Sunday)' },
    { label: 'Est. Cost', value: 'Near $0' },
    { label: 'Skill Level', value: 'Beginner' },
  ],
};
---

<Layout title="Compost Barrels | Projects | Tested by Tom" description="Two failed rain barrels get a second life as a dual-rotation compost system. Ongoing experiment — honest updates as it develops.">
<style>
  main {
    max-width: 860px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 2.5rem 1.25rem 5rem;
    font-family: 'Lato', sans-serif;
    color: var(--brown);
  }

  .back-link {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.4rem;
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: #7a6050;
    text-decoration: none;
    margin-bottom: 1.75rem;
    transition: color 0.2s;
  }
  .back-link:hover { color: var(--rust); }

  .project-header {
    background: var(--brown);
    color: var(--cream);
    padding: 2rem 2.25rem 1.75rem;
    border-radius: 2px;
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .status-row {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.75rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.9rem;
  }

  .status-badge {
    font-size: 0.65rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.15em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    padding: 0.25rem 0.65rem;
    border-radius: 2px;
    background: #e8f0eb;
    color: #2d4a3e;
  }

  .project-tag {
    font-size: 0.65rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.15em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--tan);
  }

  .project-header h1 {
    font-family: 'Fraunces', serif;
    font-size: clamp(1.4rem, 4vw, 2.1rem);
    font-weight: 700;
    line-height: 1.2;
    color: #fff;
    margin-bottom: 0.6rem;
  }

  .project-header .subtitle {
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    color: rgba(245,240,232,0.75);
    font-style: italic;
    font-family: 'Fraunces', serif;
  }

  .spec-bar {
    background: var(--cream);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-top: none;
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    margin-bottom: 2.5rem;
  }

  .spec-item {
    flex: 1 1 120px;
    padding: 1rem 1.25rem;
    border-right: 1px solid var(--border);
  }
  .spec-item:last-child { border-right: none; }

  .spec-label {
    font-size: 0.65rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--rust);
    display: block;
    margin-bottom: 0.2rem;
  }

  .spec-value {
    font-family: 'Fraunces', serif;
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--brown);
  }

  .log-section h2 {
    font-family: 'Fraunces', serif;
    font-size: 0.7rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.18em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--rust);
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.6rem;
  }

  .log-section h2::after {
    content: '';
    flex: 1;
    height: 1px;
    background: var(--border);
  }

  .log-entry {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 120px 1fr;
    gap: 0 2rem;
    margin-bottom: 2.5rem;
    padding-bottom: 2.5rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
  }

  .log-entry:last-child {
    border-bottom: none;
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .log-date {
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: #7a6050;
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
    padding-top: 0.2rem;
    font-style: italic;
  }

  .log-label {
    font-size: 0.65rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--rust);
    margin-bottom: 0.4rem;
  }

  .log-content h3 {
    font-family: 'Fraunces', serif;
    font-size: 1.2rem;
    color: var(--brown);
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
    line-height: 1.3;
  }

  .log-content p {
    font-size: 0.93rem;
    line-height: 1.75;
    color: #3a2a1a;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  .log-content p:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }

  .log-content ul {
    margin: 0.5rem 0 1rem 1.25rem;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    color: #3a2a1a;
    line-height: 1.65;
  }

  .log-content li { margin-bottom: 0.3rem; }

  .spec-block {
    background: var(--cream);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-left: 3px solid var(--rust);
    padding: 1rem 1.25rem;
    margin: 1rem 0;
    border-radius: 0 2px 2px 0;
  }

  .spec-block.tip {
    border-left-color: #2d4a3e;
  }

  .spec-block-title {
    font-size: 0.65rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--rust);
    margin-bottom: 0.6rem;
  }

  .spec-block.tip .spec-block-title {
    color: #2d4a3e;
  }

  .spec-block p {
    font-size: 0.88rem !important;
    color: #5a4030 !important;
    margin-bottom: 0 !important;
  }

  .two-col {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: 1rem;
    margin: 1rem 0;
  }

  .col-block {
    background: var(--cream);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding: 1rem 1.25rem;
    border-radius: 2px;
  }

  .col-block-title {
    font-size: 0.65rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--brown);
    margin-bottom: 0.6rem;
  }

  .col-block ul {
    margin: 0 0 0 1rem !important;
    font-size: 0.88rem !important;
  }

  .col-block.yes { border-top: 3px solid #2d4a3e; }
  .col-block.no { border-top: 3px solid var(--rust); }
  .col-block.yes .col-block-title { color: #2d4a3e; }
  .col-block.no .col-block-title { color: var(--rust); }

  @media (max-width: 580px) {
    .log-entry {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 0.25rem;
    }
    .log-date { margin-bottom: 0.5rem; }
    .spec-item { flex: 1 1 100px; }
    .two-col { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
  }
</style>

<main>
  <a href="/projects" class="back-link">← All Projects</a>

  <div class="project-header">
    <div class="status-row">
      <span class="status-badge">In Progress</span>
      <span class="project-tag">Composting · Backyard · Sustainability</span>
    </div>
    <h1>Failed Rain Barrels → Compost Barrels</h1>
    <p class="subtitle">Two barrels that never became a rain collection system find a better purpose. A first attempt at composting — documented honestly.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="spec-bar">
    {project.specs.map(spec => (
      <div class="spec-item">
        <span class="spec-label">{spec.label}</span>
        <span class="spec-value">{spec.value}</span>
      </div>
    ))}
  </div>

  <div class="log-section">
    <h2>Project Log</h2>

    <div class="log-entry">
      <div class="log-date">Spring 2026</div>
      <div class="log-content">
        <div class="log-label">Entry 01 — Setup</div>
        <h3>From Rain Barrels to Compost Barrels</h3>

        <p>
          The original plan was two rain barrels along the back of the garage, feeding a garden through gravity. That pivoted to a bucket garden, which left two large barrels sitting around doing nothing. I've always wanted to compost but never knew where to start. Turns out the barrels were already halfway there.
        </p>

        <p>
          The conversion was straightforward: 10 holes drilled in the bottom for drainage, and 10 more holes in a ring around the outside for aeration. The lids clamp on and off — important for keeping pests out when food scraps go in, and for easy access on turn day.
        </p>

        <div class="spec-block">
          <div class="spec-block-title">The Two-Barrel Rotation Plan</div>
          <p>Barrel 1 is the active barrel — scraps go in here weekly. Once it's full, it gets left alone to finish composting while Barrel 2 becomes the new active barrel. By the time Barrel 2 is full, Barrel 1 should be ready to use. Continuous output, no waiting.</p>
        </div>

        <h3 style="margin-top: 1.5rem;">How Barrel 1 is Layered</h3>

        <p>Starting from the bottom up:</p>

        <ul>
          <li><strong>Base layer:</strong> Small sticks and pine needles — allows drainage and airflow off the bottom</li>
          <li><strong>Brown layer:</strong> Last fall's leaves — carbon material to balance the food scraps</li>
          <li><strong>Green layer:</strong> Food scraps (coming once the clamps arrive)</li>
        </ul>

        <div class="two-col">
          <div class="col-block yes">
            <div class="col-block-title">✓ Goes In</div>
            <ul>
              <li>Fruit and vegetable scraps</li>
              <li>Coffee grounds and filters</li>
              <li>Eggshells</li>
              <li>Dry leaves</li>
              <li>Grass clippings</li>
              <li>Cardboard (torn small)</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <div class="col-block no">
            <div class="col-block-title">✗ Stays Out</div>
            <ul>
              <li>Meat and fish</li>
              <li>Dairy products</li>
              <li>Oily or greasy food</li>
              <li>Cooked food with sauces</li>
              <li>Pet waste</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="spec-block tip">
          <div class="spec-block-title">Current Status</div>
          <p>Barrel 1 is layered and ready. Waiting on the lid clamps to arrive before adding food scraps — keeping pests out is the priority. Weekly Sunday stirring reminder is set. Food scraps start once the lid is secured.</p>
        </div>

      </div>
    </div>

  </div>
</main>
</Layout>
